{{!--
  The leveled-condition row, shared by the character sheet and the NPC
  statblock.

  It is a partial because the two had drifted: the character sheet learned the
  per-condition ceiling and the disease floor, and the NPC sheet — which
  inherits the very same context, since `FalloutNpcSheet` overrides only
  `PARTS` and `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` — kept a hardcoded `min="0" max="10"` and used
  neither. One copy of the markup means the next correction cannot land on only
  one of them.

  Two things this row reads that a flat `min`/`max` cannot express:

  - `floor` — levels a disease pins in place until it is cured (Dysentery's four
    Dehydration, Parasites' four Hunger). It is the input's minimum, and the row
    says so with the lock rather than silently refusing a smaller number.
  - `max` — the printed track's ceiling, which is *not* the schema's: the schema
    has no maximum at all. Ten is the convention for the conditions whose tracks
    stop there, and `null` for Short Circuit, which doubles on becoming wet
    (pg 135) with no cap. A flat ten stored such a value fine and then refused to
    let a GM type it back in, which is the worst of both — the number was real
    and the sheet would not accept it.
--}}
{{#each conditions}}
<label class="condition{{#if floor}} locked{{/if}}"
       {{#if floor}}title="{{localize 'FALLOUT.Diseases.floorHint' floor=floor}}"{{/if}}>
  <span>{{label}}{{#if floor}} <i class="fas fa-lock"></i>{{/if}}</span>
  <input type="number" name="system.conditions.{{key}}" value="{{value}}"
         min="{{floor}}" {{#if max}}max="{{max}}"{{/if}} />
</label>
{{/each}}
